<title>COLOMBIA: Colombia to raise $100 mln in bankruptcy sales.</title>
<headline>Colombia to raise $100 mln in bankruptcy sales.</headline>
<dateline>BOGOTA 1997-07-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Colombia hopes to raise nearly $100 million by selling off businesses that have gone bankrupt since the government began lowering its protectionist trade barriers seven years ago, a government spokesman said Tuesday.</p>
<p>At least 60 companies will be put on the block, including auto distributors, construction companies and clothing manufacturers, Maria Cristina Mora, a bankruptcy analyst with the government's Corporate Superintendency told Reuters.</p>
</text>
